  "raw": {
    "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/6acbdb5fce3bee6d3c2afb7f": {
      "title": "Admission Counselor/Assistant Director of Music Recruitment",
      "description": "LutherCollege-Admission Counselor/Assistant Director of Music Recruitment Admission Counselor/Assistant Director of Music Recruitment Luther College Admissions Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description Wage: $36,000 - $50,000 SUMMARY : The Admission Counselor / Assistant Director of Music Recruitment is responsible for recruiting, counseling, and managing relationships with prospective Luther College students interested in music.  Serving as the primary Admissions contact for prospective music students, this position develops and implements a strategic music recruitment plan in collaboration with Music and Enrollment leaders. Responsibilities also include individual college counseling (for all prospective students), group presentations, proactive communication, participation in campus visit programs, and evaluation of music activities and marketing strategies, with recommendations to strengthen effectiveness and outcomes. They will be involved in the creation of music marketing materials, enrollment reporting, and broader relationship building with key constituents. The position also serves as a liaison between Admissions and the Music Department and coordinates key components of the music scholarship audition process.  Extensive travel during the spring, summer, and fall recruitment seasons is required. ESSENTIAL DUTIES and RESPONSIBILITIES : Recruitment and Enrollment Manage and implement an annual recruitment plan for students who are interested in music. Build and maintain relationships with prospective students and their families, high school counselors, community-based organizations, and other key influencers. Plan and conduct school visits, attend college fairs and community events, and represent the college at other recruitment events. Many of these will have a focus around music however, some will not. Monitor performance indicators (i.e. # of auditions) and adjust recruitment strategies accordingly based on enrollment goals and market conditions. Communicate with students and families via email, text, phone, virtual meetings, and in-person interactions. Collaborate with Enrollment colleagues and campuswide partners around visitor schedules and student cases. Student and Family Engagement Conduct admissions conversations with individual students and families. Provide accurate and timely information regarding academic programs, student life, financial aid, scholarships, and the admissions process. Assess and respond to student needs and opportunities throughout the recruitment process, especially for those interested in music at Luther. Admissions Operations and Counseling Maintain accurate records regarding recruitment travel, admission and scholarships. Utilize the institution’s CRM (Slate) for admissions processes, communication, and data analysis. Ensure student information for all Dorian participants is added to Slate and perform outreach. Events and Campus Visits Participate in the planning and execution of campus visit programs, off-campus student events, and other recruitment activities. Assist with campus visit coverage, including counselor chats and event presentations. Travel to represent Luther Music and host the Luther Music booth at set conventions (typically 7 – 10 per calendar year). Organize recruitment travel for music related conferences and conventions. Strategic Projects and Campus Partnerships Serve as liaison to the Music department and Dorian-related programming. Execute music scholarship protocols, audition planning (in-person & virtual) and logistics for music auditions. This may include partnering with Visit Event staff and Faculty to schedule auditions. Maintain inventory and ordering for Luther Music items shared with prospective music students Manage webpage content for the prospective music student pages on Luther’s site. In collaboration with Enrollment & Marketing leaders, update print materials with a music focus for distribution to prospective musicians. Lead or contribute to strategic projects supporting enrollment goals, student recruitment, and visitor engagement. Oversee mailing projects for the Music dept. posters and All-State letters. Perform other duties as assigned. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES : 1-2 student Ambassadors with a focus in music EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE and SKILLS : EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE and SKILLS: Education : Bachelor’s degree in any major required. Knowledge of Music and Music Education is essential. Must have strong communication, teamwork, and organizational skills. Familiarity with liberal arts colleges and fluency in a second language are desirable. Experience : One year of relevant experience preferred. Experience in sales, marketing, communication, counseling, or education is a plus. Strong written, and verbal skills. Must be enthusiastic, goal-oriented, self-motivated, team-oriented, and capable of representing Luther energetically and positively to prospective students and their parents. Experience working with Slate (or a similar CRM), Google Suite, and Microsoft is preferred. Candidates must have a valid driver's license and a driving record that will enable them to be insured through the college. Ability to cultivate and develop inclusive and equitable working relationships with students, faculty, staff, alumni, parents, and friends of the college PHYSICAL DEMANDS and WORK ENVIRONMENT: This position requires traveling on a regular basis throughout the year.  Occasional overnight and weekend travel is required throughout the year.  When in the office: sedentary work.  Sitting, standing, and walking in well-lighted and well-ventilated office involved Job ID 13260153076 | Posted on October 12, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"
    },
    "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/6aaadf2fce3bee6d3c264446": {
      "title": "CFL Technician",
      "description": "LutherCollege-CFL Technician CFL Technician Luther College Other Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description SUMMARY The CFL Technician is a full-time position and offers technical support, collaborative planning with the Head CFL Technician, and quality customer service for all events in the Center for Faith and Life. Wage: $16.64 - $19.58 ESSENTIAL DUTIES and RESPONSIBILITIES Offer services to Center for Faith and Life users, campus event planners, and off- campus guests including all sound, lighting, and audio–visual needs. Determine users’ technical needs and explain technical options available. Work with the Head CFL Technician to coordinate space needs, availability, and planning for upcoming events. Uphold a standard of excellence in technical support for the CFL. Provide general support for Programming & Outreach. Assist as necessary with building management for the Center for Faith and Life. SHARED DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES (All Technicians) Provide technical assistance and general support for all events in the CFL Main Hall and Recital Hall for conferences, campus-wide events, the Center Stage Series, Christmas at Luther, festivals, concerts, college ministry services, camps, conventions and other special projects for the academic year and summer conference season. Offer technical direction for events, including implementation of contracts and riders. Read and apply light and stage plots from touring companies. Act as contact for the technical end of productions. Assess and arbitrate production costs including the rental and billing of additional equipment and assistance. Set up truss, curtains, lighting and sound system, and other multimedia equipment as needed.  Load in, set up, and load out guest sets and equipment. Responsible for all aspects of sound reinforcement and theatrical lighting including design, set up, operation, trouble shooting, repair, replacement and inventory. Record lectures, concerts, recitals, and worship services in the Center for Faith and as requested. Responsible for technical support and set up of College Ministry Sunday worship and weekday chapel services. Assist with other Programming & Outreach duties when needed. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES Assist Head CFL Technician in directing and offering guidance to student technicians, student volunteers, and members of the Performing Arts Committee. EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE and SKILLS Education Bachelor’s or Associate's Degree preferred. Experience At least two years of experience working with audio systems and/or theatrical lighting, including design, set up, focusing and repair, and multimedia resources. Familiarity with a Yamaha DM7 soundboard and Dante networking is preferred. Skills Commitment to customer service. Skills in leadership, team building, and analytical problem solving. Strong organizational and verbal skills Ability to work independently and with a team Ability to cultivate and develop inclusive and equitable working relationships with students, staff, alumni, parents, and friends of the college PHYSICAL DEMANDS and WORK ENVIRONMENT Must be able to work at heights on ladders, catwalks, and a personnel lift. Must be able to handle heavy lifting. Must be willing to work long and irregular hours including nights and weekends. Must be able to climb stairs, no elevator on premises. Mostly indoor work. Air conditioned in summer and warm in winter. Job ID 13062577229 | Posted on September 17, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"
    },
    "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/6aa865bdce3bee6d3c25ed1b": {
      "title": "Transfer Credit Coordinator",
      "description": "LutherCollege-Transfer Credit Coordinator Transfer Credit Coordinator Luther College Other Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description Description Salary: $33,500-$44,600 The Transfer Credit Coordinator plays a crucial role in facilitating the transfer of academic credit of students from dual enrollment programs, community colleges, other four-year colleges and universities, and alternative credit sources to Luther College. The Transfer Credit Coordinator evaluates, processes, and posts academic credits from prior schools so students can apply them toward a new degree program. Reporting to the Registrar and working closely with academic department and program heads, this position ensures accurate and timely recording of transfer credit decisions and supports students, advisors, and faculty in understanding transfer credit policies and procedures. This position is responsible for the maintenance of transfer course equivalency tables in the Colleague student information system as well as in other web-based applications and transfer credit pathways. Transcript reading software will be utilized and maintained by this position to ensure consistency, integrity, and accuracy transfer crediting. The person holding this position documents the needs of transfer students and communicates trends to their supervisor and other stakeholders at the college for continuous improvement. This role will also include involvement in Registrar’s Office tasks, and participating in admissions and advising related activities and events in support of incoming students. Duties and Responsibilities Manage Transfer Equivalencies: Conduct assessment of transcripts, course descriptions, and syllabi to determine transfer credit, contacting stakeholders for approval as needed, and entering into the student information system. Maintain the transfer course equivalency data base and update the student information system (Transferology, Colleague). Utilize transcript reading software to ensure consistency, integrity, and accuracy in transfer crediting. Research and review programs and courses from other academic institutions, contacting appropriate stakeholders as needed. Make recommendations for the determination of course equivalencies to the Registrar. Participate in the development and maintenance of transfer pathways and articulation agreements with colleges with representatives of the Office of Academic Affairs.  Provide timely and accurate information in the development of articulation resources. Communicate with stakeholders: Act as a focal point for questions from academic advisors, the Director of Advising and other stakeholders regarding credits that have the potential to transfer. Communicate and respond to student inquiries about transfer credit evaluation results and provide guidance on next steps. Refer students to other support offices on campus as needed. Provide excellent and timely customer service pertaining to degree exploration, transfer credit and syllabi evaluation, and degree completion pathways or scenarios. Coordinate with Admissions Office staff and other stakeholders to respond quicklyto queries regarding course evaluation and transfer credits.Must be familiar with Luther College majors, minors, and concentrations as well as Core Curriculum (general education) requirements. Maintain positive collaborative relationships with Academic Affairs, Admissions, Advising, faculty, the Center for Global Learning and other campus stakeholders. Participate in all aspects of the duties and responsibilities of the Office of the Registrar. Perform other duties as assigned by the Registrar. Education, Experience, Skills, and Work Environment: Bachelor's degree is required. Two or more years of work experience in higher education preferred. Familiarity with academic policies and procedures of a college or university, preferably a liberal arts curriculum. Knowledge of FERPA and records compliance in an academic setting. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of populations representing diverse backgrounds, cultures, life experiences, and abilities. Ability to cultivate and develop inclusive and equitable working relationships with students, faculty, staff, parents, and representatives of other academic institutions. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills required to meet with students, staff, faculty and parents. Strong organizational skills with exceptional attention to detail and ability to manage multiple priorities. Ability to work effectively as part of a team in a service environment with frequent interruptions (e-mail, chat, telephone, and walk-in traffic) and still meet deadlines. Ability to work independently and to make decisions based on general guidelines. Proficiency using Microsoft Office programs, Google Suite, and competence with a variety of software applications including CRMs, databases, form management, etc. Evidence of previous project management certification/experience, preferred. Knowledge of student information systems, preferred. Familiarity with international educational systems, grading scales, curricula, and transcripts, preferred. Physical Demands and Work Environment: Work is often performed in an office environment with frequent in-person interactions and requires the ability to operate standard office equipment. Involves sitting for long periods of time at desk/office. Position will require occasional evening and weekend activities to support student registration, commencement weekend and/or admissions events and programming. Ability to lift 15 lbs (student records; table set up at events) Job ID 13044896881 | Posted on September 24, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"
    },
    "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/6a9f30ffce3bee6d3c24d71b": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant (English; Modern Languages and Cultures; Paideia; and Religion)",
      "description": "LutherCollege-Administrative Assistant (English; Modern Languages and Cultures; Paideia; and Religion) Administrative Assistant (English; Modern Languages and Cultures; Paideia; and Religion) Luther College Paideia Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description Job Title: Administrative Assistant (English; Modern Languages and Cultures; Paideia; and Religion) FLSA Status: Non-Exempt FTE: .83 (10 months) Wage: $14.01-$16.48 SUMMARY: The Paideia Program and the academic departments of English, MLC (Modern Languages and Cultures), and Religion require a highly motivated, detail-oriented Administrative Assistant with strong interpersonal and written communication skills for a full-time position during the academic year and one summer month ESSENTIAL DUTIES and RESPONSIBILITIES: Communication and coordination among faculty and students: Managing the Paideia Office and the Language Learning Center and all their contents and people Serving as the first point of contact for the Paideia Office and the Language Learning Center Hiring, training, and coordinating supervision of student workers, including the management of time cards Organization: Maintaining the organizational manual of events, tasks, deadlines, etc. Organizing academic events, including lectures and senior paper presentations Helping make travel and other arrangements for guest speakers Maintaining Paideia faculty program calendar and calendars for student worker Scheduling rooms in Main for meetings, tutoring sessions, quizzes/tests Maintaining and retrieving electronic records Ordering departmental supplies Managing financial paperwork (e.g., for honoraria and reimbursements for guest speakers, department budgets) Program reviews: Assisting with the collection and collation of materials for program reviews Publications: print and web Assisting with the publication of the Paideia Reader Assisting with maintenance of web pages Texts and Permissions Managing Paideia book orders and desk copies Managing copyright permissions for course packs SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: Coordinating supervision of student workers EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE and SKILLS: Education: Associates Degree required. Experience: 5 years applicable experience required. Ability to work independently and take the lead on designated projects Ability to learn and use various software, including Microsoft Office and Google Suite Ability to cultivate and develop inclusive and equitable working relationships with students, faculty, staff, alumni, parents, and friends of the college PHYSICAL DEMANDS and WORK ENVIRONMENT: Office environment with frequent faculty and student traffic Ability to multitask and prioritize in a busy office environment This position operates in a professional, collaborative office environment. The role requires efficient and extensive use of computers, telephones, and other office equipment. This role operates fully on-campus in Decorah, Iowa but occasional remote work days may be available as needed for personal reasons. Work requires exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or the ability to lift, carry, push or pull, or otherwise move objects with a limited amount of force. Job ID 12991727204 | Posted on September 10, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"
