    "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/69d7b75daa7bfffa4b456380": {
      "title": "Boiler Operator & Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "LutherCollege-Boiler Operator & Maintenance Technician Boiler Operator & Maintenance Technician Facilities Services Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description SUMMARY Operate the Luther College Heating Plant in such a manner as to provide a constant uninterrupted supply of steam to the Luther campus. Maintain and validate automation systems for proper and accurate operation.  Help to analyze data to determine operational savings. Perform this service at all times in a safe method to insure personal safety and safety to all Luther College faculty, staff, students and guests. Wage Range: $17.34-$20.40 ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Operate boilers safely while being alert and able to handle emergencies. Perform proper water tests; boiler, softener, and condensate. Work safely with chemicals, steam, and 190+ --degree water. Maintain all plant daily records. Do required pool tests, record keeping, and filter maintenance, especially prior to pool opening. Test and maintain all steam lines to buildings. Test cooling towers for proper chemicals and operation. Record operational data for chillers and water softeners. Review Automated Logic building automation system for: Proper set points Verify operational parameters Check actual values to reported values Re-commission controls on a schedule Log operational data for further system cost review Perform preventative work or repairs from the work order system Plumbing Requests Mechanical/HVAC Requests Replacing lamps, shutting off circuits, resetting circuit breakers, etc Other requests that may come up Handle all types of work requests on weekends that come up Welding/brazing for college repair work Metal fabrication for needs on campus Assist in unloading fuel transports. Other work as assigned. SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES May need to supervise student workers. QUALIFICATIONS To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skills, and/or ability required.  Must be able to read, follow and give direction.  Must be able to diagnose problems and determine an appropriate solution.  Must be able to read and interpret blueprints for troubleshooting. EDUCATION and/or EXPERIENCE High School Diploma required. Mechanical or electrical background Experience with boiler operation Will need computer skills for spreadsheets, monitoring computerized building automation system, e-mail, etc. Ability to cultivate and develop inclusive and equitable working relationships with students, faculty, staff, alumni, parents, and friends of the college. CERTIFICATES, LICENSES, REGISTRATIONS Driver’s License. Boiler Operator 1 (ability to obtain through Luther) Boiler Operator 2 (ability to obtain through Luther) Certified Pool Operator (CPO) (ability to obtain through Luther) Private School or College Routine Maintenance Specialty License (ability to obtain through Luther). PHYSICAL DEMANDS Mobility: ability to ascend and descend ladders of various heights, stairs, scaffolding and ramps; not be afraid of heights; walk or stand for extended periods of time. Lifting: ability to lift and hold 75 pounds, frequently lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects up to 50 pounds, lifting and holding 10-25 pounds above head. Dexterity: must have a full range of motion in the upper extremities; manual dexterity to operate equipment including scissors lifts, power tools and hand tools; ability to work for extended periods with arms above head. WORK ENVIRONMENT Inside and outside buildings---working in temperatures that range from heated rooms to outside temperatures of extreme heat and cold. High noise levels. Extreme temperature changes. Buildings and grounds are smoke/tobacco free. Shifts up to 12 hrs. Night shift possible. Overtime may be required. Will need to work rotating weekends and be on call. Some areas may be poorly ventilated or heavily congested. Exposure to potentially hazardous chemicals, noise, dust and fumes. Required to work in restricted places which may require stooping, bending and kneeling. Job ID 11710587411 | Posted on September 22, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"
    },
    "https://go.jobflows.co/LutherCollege/69d7b5a5aa7bfffa4b4561b1": {
      "title": "Custodial Staff",
      "description": "LutherCollege-Custodial Staff Custodial Staff Facilities Services Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible APPLY NOW Job Description SUMMARY: Ensure campus spaces are safe and clean for students, employees, and guests. Positions available in academic and residential buildings to support student life, academic operations, and other events on campus. Starting Wage:  $14.00 - $15.00 per hour Full-time and part-time Positions Available Positions available in first, second, and third shift Shift differential pay +$.75/hour or +$1.50/hour Opportunities to advance to Custodial Lead +$1.50/hour ESSENTIAL DUTIES and RESPONSIBILITIES: The custodial staff maintains building appearance and cleanliness in all areas; lobbies, entrances, classrooms, offices, hallways, kitchens, conference rooms, staircases, study lounges; restrooms, and shower rooms. Custodial duties will consist of but not limited to: Unlock/lock building and turn on/off lights Sweep Mop Vacuum Empty trash receptacles and dispose of trash Clean glass Dust surface areas Disinfect fixtures Annual deep cleaning Assist with set-up for campus events Snow removal Maintain outside entrances year round Recycling Clean restroom and show-room facilities Floor care Other duties as assigned SUPERVISORY RESPONSIBILITIES: If this particular position is a lead position, you will provide guidance and organization to other team members in your building You may be asked to direct student and support student workers EDUCATION, EXPERIENCE and SKILLS: Education: High School diploma and/or equivalent preferred but not required Experience: Must be detail orientated and have good time management and organizational skills. Basic computer knowledge and operation Proven ability to work with others Must be able to read sufficiently to follow instructions, ability to mix appropriate chemical dilution ratio and understand directions for use. Ability to cultivate and develop inclusive and equitable working relationships with students, faculty, staff, alumni, parents, and friends of the college PHYSICAL DEMANDS and WORK ENVIRONMENT: Mobility: walk or stand for extended periods of time Lifting: ability to lift and carry 50 pounds Dexterity:  must have a full range of motion including bending, stretching, lifting, and kneeling. Be available for scheduled shift Overtime may be required Inside and outside of buildings, spaces may or may not be air conditioned Exposure to potentially hazardous chemicals, noise, dust and fumes Required to work in restricted places which may require stooping, bending and kneeling Buildings and grounds are smoke free Job ID 11710495358 | Posted on May 12, 2026 Share this job Facebook Twitter LinkedIn Related Jobs Lead Custodian Facilities Services Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible SUMMARY:   Ensure campus spaces are safe and clean for students, employees, and guests. Positions available in academic and residential buildings to support student life, academic operations, and ot Boiler Operator & Maintenance Technician Facilities Services Decorah, IA Benefits Eligible SUMMARY   Operate the Luther College Heating Plant in such a manner as to provide a constant uninterrupted supply of steam to the Luther campus. Maintain and validate automation systems for proper a Luther College does not discriminate on the basis of race, sex, color, religion, age, national origin, marital status, disability, veteran status, genetic information, sexual orientation, gender identity or any other reason prohibited by law in provision of employment opportunities and benefits. Luther College | Powered by Jobflows for monday.com Work OS"
